        <mxCell id="ybpy1l-WJgSBDr3oyrRi-19" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" value="&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Composition over inheritance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;:&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;A robot body is (in our case) made up from an arm actuator and an&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;a gripper actuator. We can swap these modules easily for different robots.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Furthermore, if we want to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;mute the gripper, use a DummyGripper, if we want to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;mute the arm, use a DummyArm. Both at the same&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;time make sense for Kinesthetic recording.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The &lt;b&gt;factory pattern&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;would make sense here, but that might&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;make it too complex for &#39;beginners&#39;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;(already designed a lot using&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;theory&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;not included in this bachelor)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="420" x="870" y="1325" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
